			<div class="content" id="post-content-4474385">
									

<p>First and foremost, I apologize if my posting came off as patronizing or intentionally demeaning. It is never my intent to be intentionally discouraging, I post that precisely because I want to make sure that new authors are aware of the resources available to them.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">Folded,&nbsp;for&nbsp;our&nbsp;mobile&nbsp;users&nbsp;-&gt;</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>I do try and check to see if the author is actually a new author, but its not a precise science. Often I have a fairly short window to try and get these links out for the new author to see, so I don't get an opportunity to really do a full history search.</p>
<p>Also, I should point out that you do not need to go through the <span style="color: green">greenlight</span> process in order to post to the main site. Everyone is free to post whatever they want, and the <span style="color: green">greenlight</span> process is not meant to prevent that. What it does is help make best use of the resources available, both to staff and to the users themselves. I know from personal experience how we can oftentimes pour a bunch of time and resources into an idea only to find that the concept was fundamentally flawed from the beginning. This is to try and help prevent that.</p>
<p>Finally, I want to thank you for continuing to try and work within the system and for putting your work out there. I realize that the post I put up wasn't exactly useful to you, but I hope that you can recognize how I am trying to help. The &quot;roadmap&quot; I put in there is my own addition, in the hopes that I can also give the authors a bit of quickie guide. I'm always open to feedback on how to make it better, more an effective tool, rather than some sort of &quot;punishment.&quot;</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

