<p>There's a couple rookie slip-ups in here, stuff like using feet measurement, the deprecated &quot;number (#)&quot; notation, and minor grammar/word errors, like &quot;region containing the entrance SCP-5000&quot;.</p>
<p>That aside, the core premise isn't immediately grabbing me (though I admit I'm kinda blase when it comes to skips that center around referencing other skips). The layout also leaves something to be desired; you've got the Navigation Procedures (which might even not be necessary) wedged smack in between the Discovery and the journals. Same goes for the little blurb about SCP-1281 trying to send its message. I'm also not sure why this is Thaumiel.</p>
<p>If you do end up reworking this, I would recommend focusing the work more, either on the expedition crew, or whatever implications you're trying to build with the tunnels full of replica SCPs, because it feels disjoint right now.</p>

