<blockquote>
<p>I'm not one to want to tailor the SCP to some story</p>
</blockquote>
<p>SCPs are inherently works of fiction, insofar as that they serve an ultimate narrative purpose more often than not. If your goals here are not to weave a cohesive narrative in with the SCP format, then you will not have an easy time here.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>the Navigation Procedures would be relevant to the study of this SCP, irrespective of its connection to the strange happenings regarding the SCP's discovery.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>What you may have failed to realize here is that every word you spend not progressing your story, building characters, adding suspense/atmosphere, or priming your readers is a word wasted. Doing things like this will destroy the pacing of your narrative and cause most of your readers to lose interest.</p>

