														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4481006">
									

<p>This is really a difference in implied creative purpose of this wiki, then. I (and I know I am not alone in this interpretation) read SCPs in the literal sense as a fictitious log of anomalous happenings in our world. It's a reference source, a database of sorts. CIA agents don't write stories into their mission reports, or hope that some compelling narrative pops out of whatever it was they were doing that is more often than not a bit mundane.</p>
<p>That being said, there is the narrative aspect. This is fiction, and fiction tends to tell stories; few would choose to peruse boring mission reports, and perhaps I am underestimating the number of people who read this sort of stuff for the stories more so than the concepts. But, as an extension of my own comment:</p>
<blockquote>
<p>I'm not one to want to tailor the SCP to some story</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Instead, I'd rather tailor the story to the SCP.</p>

